  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1123 AM CDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nMild and dry conditions are expected Monday into early Tuesday as\nwe look upstream for the next active system. That system will be \na much more potent low pressure center that will bring soaking \nrainfall across the area by midweek. Deep moisture, gusty breezes,\nand strong lift will develop by Tuesday evening, bringing a high \nchance for showers across the area Tuesday evening through \nWednesday. Models are varied with the exact details of this storm\nsystem, but models are confident we will have potential for heavy\nshowers at times, especially Wednesday. The system looks quite \ndynamic, so some storms should be expected. However, the shear and\ninstability parameters do not appear to line up for much of a \nsevere storm risk. It is something we will have to keep an eye on.\n\nWhile this weekend's rain event looks like a potential under-\nachiever, the midweek storm system could be an over-achiever.\nWidespread 1 to 2 inch rainfall totals are expected, but some \nspots could pick up more than 2 inches. That would certainly not \nend the drought, but it would pause the trend for a while. \n\nSome showers may linger Thursday and perhaps early Friday as \ntrailing troughiness impacts the region. It looks like dry and \nseasonable air will come in later Friday, setting us up for a \nnice fall weekend.",
